            "review_title": "Review at Sushi Shinkon",
            "review_text": "Tung Tran\nHo Chi Minh City, Vietnam4 contributions\n0\nSurprisingly excellent new omakase spot in town - mesmerizing sushi but not for a casual price tag\nJan 2023 • Friends\nTried this one out of curiousity from an instagram advert since all the omakase spots in Saigon are no strange places to me, a year living in Japan has made me a seasoned and hard to please Japanese food eater.\n\nSurprisingly excellent. Full Japanese-educated team of very talented chefs. I have had food from chef Linh in District 7 before but needless to say he has improved massively at Shinkon.\n\nLocation and place: 9/10 - central location with valet parking, unfortunately you can’t park here hence the 9. In the middle of bursting Nguyen Hue street, sophisticated interior design. Would have appreciated some more width but you can’t ask for much in district 1 to be darnk.\n\nFood: 9/10 - top notch ingredient (trust me on this as I have spent my youth scrouching for fish markets in Tokyo), very risk but well put combination of food - noted my love for the treasure box which is a improvising combination of the chef. Bare in mind tradional sushi eaters should let the chef know otherwise he will get creative (which is more my thing). Food can easily rival with Sushi Rei. My only negative feedback would be the wait some time for the food, but after 3rd visit they have improved. Oh and excellent Sake choices, some very fine Dassai bottles.\n\nStaff: 7/10 - all good manners but the staff are quite new and still to be trained (they are still in soft opening I believe) - but nothing majorly bad as in omakase you mainly interact with the chef\n\nPrice- 7/10 - menus starting from above 2 million to above 4 million have put this restaurant at the very expensive end. With drinks and tax you are looking at 3-4 million Vnd for a fine evening. But with the location and quality and I am happy so far, but would save this for a few special occasions.\nRead more\nWritten February 5, 2023",
